{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1559105-common-curseborne-questions-and-answers","id":1559105,"title":"Common Curseborne Questions (and Answers!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-29T15:52:19-07:00","id":1559105,"title":"Common Curseborne Questions (and Answers!)","content":"Hello! I noticed that the Curseborne Core Book sometimes raises some questions surrounding mechanics that are left unanswered or unclear. I aim with this to help clarify as many of those rulings as possible.<br /> <br /> <u>Important Note</u><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I AM NOT A DEVELOPER OR WRITER FOR CURSEBORNE.</li> <li>THIS IS NOT A DIG AT THE DEVELOPERS OR WRITERS.</li> <li>I LOVE CURSEBORNE AND WANT AS MANY PEOPLE TO ENJOY IT AS POSSIBLE.</li> </ol><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Clarifications</u></span></span></b><br /> These are questions I see frequently asked, and ones that have solid answers (either given by the writers, common sense, or other reliable sources).<ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How does Advantage (182) work?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Advantage\u2019s Enhancement ignores all normal limits for Enhancement, aka: no stacking, caps at +3 for a single source, and the cap of +5 total.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is Robust and Light in the Armor table (215)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Robust = Exquisite Material, Light = Fitted.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where is the Loophole Edge (238) and how much does it cost?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The header is invisible, and costs 2 Edge dots (237).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is the Ethereal attunement in the Incorporeal Quality (341)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ethereal refers to the Transcendent weapon tag (231).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What do you roll for perception?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival + Composure is a good base, but many different skill/attribute combinations could apply.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What do you roll for sneaking?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Larceny + (Cunning or Dexterity) vs the target\u2019s Integrity is a good base, but many different skill/attribute combinations could apply.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Common Questions</u></span></span></b><br /> These are questions I see frequently asked that I do NOT have solid answers for, but have unofficial solutions nevertheless. All of the rulings below try to fit the text as best as possible, however, many of them start to lean into house rule territory. Feel free to ignore or change whatever you need to best fit your table.<ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is activating the Hungry\u2019s Undead Strength (68) a reflexive action or a simple action?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cIf the type of action isn\u2019t specified, it\u2019s assumed to be a simple action\u201d (193).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say that a Hungry can activate as many instances of Undead Strength as they want as part of a single simple action. If they want to activate more on a later turn, it would require another simple action.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do you heal from an injury stemmed from a bane or the Deprived status effect as a Hungry (68)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say as long as the Hungry is no longer suffering from the bane or Deprived status effect (such as after the scene ends or after successfully feeding) they can heal said injury using Undead Strength.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do the victims of an Ascetic, Black Heart, Gaki, or Vorare Major Path Hunger feeding suffer a status effect (70)? There isn\u2019t one specified.</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say yes, the victim should at least suffer the Drained status effect like Blood Thirst (67).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is activating the Outcast\u2019s Slipping Off the Mask (94) a reflexive action or a simple action?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cIf the type of action isn\u2019t specified, it\u2019s assumed to be a simple action\u201d (193).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say that they do not need to spend an action to slip off the mask if they are within a liminality, as it happens automatically.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do Outcasts choose their tags on character creation or each time they activate Slipping Off the Mask (94)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say the player chooses the tags each time they activate Slipping Off the Mask, allowing for the adaptation of tags for the situation at hand.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do certain Primals (Eight Hands, Hydes) have 1 or 2 natural armor in their shifts since they have Padded x1 (117)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say they only have 1 natural armor to make things even across all Families. However, I can see either way.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can a Sorcerer use Spell Mimicry (140) on antagonists?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerers can only use the spell Drain Quality (281) to steal Qualities and Dread Powers. However, the Dread Power Potion Junkie (345) allows an antagonist to cast a collection of Accursed spells, which I say can be individually mimicked (meeting the usual requirements of seeing the spell cast in the same scene and is a Sorcerer/Shared spell).</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do Sorcerers gain two curse dice when using Sacrifices (140) to sacrifice a Major Path Sacrifice (141) to resolve their Damnation (244)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say yes, once from the sacrifice itself and another for triggering the resolution effect on their Damnation.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do Complications stack (180)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cSome actions may come with multiple Complications due to an ability adding to an action that already had one applied. In these situations, buying off the largest Complication resolves all Complications on the action.\u201d (The World Below 117) <i>(I know this isn't from Curseborne, but it is a good ruling)</i></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I agree that buying off the largest Complication to resolve the smaller ones is good, but I split Complications into Personal Complications and Area Complications, which need to be bought off separately.</span></span><ul><li><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ex. John is suffering from Bleeding (minor personal complication) and Agony (moderate personal complication). In the area, there is Dread (minor area complication) and Disturbing (moderate area complication). He would need to buy off the highest of each, resulting in 2 hits for personal and 2 hits for area, totaling needing 4 hits to buy off both.</span></span></i></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Does Armor stack (203)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I only allow one magical instance and one mundane/worn instance at a time. <i>(ex. If a character is wearing both a kevlar vest and a suit of armor, take the higher armor rating out of the two and ignore the other)</i></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do Armor Tags such as Exquisite Material, Fitted, Impenetrable, or Spiked (214) still apply after the armor\u2019s injury boxes have been filled?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say yes, unless the armor is hit with the Sunder trick or other narrative circumstances happen to disable the armor\u2019s tags.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do clashes add an Attribute to the pool (248)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say no, since this is a case where it flat-out states the dice pool instead of mentioning a Skill to be paired with an Attribute (187). </span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can the Skill listed for clashes be changed (248)?</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I say yes, this can be done without an Advancement as long as it still makes sense for the spell.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}